  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "A byte is able to store 5 trits, but you need to encode them in a more complex manner.\n\nHave you considered doing this to save almost 20% memory at the cost of some bitwise operations per lookup?\n\nPossible techniques:\n- just add them together, multiplying each time by 3\n- 5 243-byte lookup tables, one for each trit\n- use smaller lookup tables and some arithmetic\n\nhttps://chatgpt.com/share/68188d60-1924-8012-a489-5b2d4bce2e21",
